-- title:
--   Level descent of the rigid chart at q = 2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with the additional hypothesis `hq2` that $q = 2$, and $M'$ is a nonzero level. The data are: a guard prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (hypotheses `hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`); a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$; a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$; an inclusion `hle` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ function field) into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ (a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, and the compatibilities recorded in that structure); a distinguished $s \in W$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with elements $\pi_0$ (lying in $A$, by `hπ`), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$; a natural number $\ell$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cutting out $A$ (`hAb`) and an element $\varpi_b$; a subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$, an algebra over $A \cap k_0 = A.\mathrm{comap}(k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q})$ in a scalar tower, with a nonzero element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$; an element $\varpi_t' \in A \cap k_0$; an ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(A\cap k_0)\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, the algebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $(A\cap k_0)[j_\ell]$; a subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ over $A \cap k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n$, $m$; an element $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal; the hypothesis `hjK` that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ lies in $K_\ell$; an element $a_0 \in A \cap k_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   The arithmetic hypotheses on this frame are: $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); $A$ lies over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$ (`hA`); $W$ is exactly the set $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$ of supersingular places (`hW`); `hR₀`, that every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is an $R_0$-integer whose $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction; `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field; `hκ`, that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$; `hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`, that $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; `hζ₀`, that $\zeta_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; `hϖtA` and `hϖt`, that $\varpi_t \in A$ and $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$; `hKb`, that $K_b$ is the bottom field, i.e. $K_b = k_0$; `hϖb`, `hϖb0`, that $\varpi_b \neq 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$; `htame`, that $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A \cap k_0$; `hξ`, that $\xi$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity; `hH₁`, that $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \cap \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\big)$; `hKℓ`, that $K_\ell$ is the base change to $k_0$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1$; `hjℓ`, that $j_\ell$ is the image of the $q$-expansion $jq$; and `hϖt'`, that $\varpi_t'$ is $\varpi_t$.
--
--   The chart hypotheses are: `hy`, that $y$ is maximal, and `hϖy`, that $\pi_0 \in y$; `hss`, that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$ (every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point); `hover`, that for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ function field whose base change is an $R_0$-integer, which is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the corresponding element of $K_\ell$ lies in the chart algebra and differs by an element of $y$ from every constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the evaluation of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ at $s$; and `hOrbit`, that any maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same specialisation property as in `hover` is carried to $y$ by a level automorphism, i.e. there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$ — the condition that $\tau$ realises, on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral expansions, the slash action of $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ after any embedding of $k_0$ in $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra and pulls $y'$ back to $y$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hS1` is the rigid-chart package (thirteen clauses, summarised here): the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$ and $B_t$ has fraction field $K_\ell$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A\cap k_0$ and $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ in $A \cap k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, cuts out $y$ on the chart algebra, and is the localisation of $B_t$ at its maximal ideal; for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A \cap k_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q$ of that residue field, with kernel the centre of $W_t$, compatible with scalars, and equivariant for the level automorphisms preserving $W_t$ through the subgroup $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup}\,q$ and its action $\mathrm{hAction}$, together with a nontriviality clause and the existence of a purely scalar companion automorphism; $B_t$ is stable under level automorphisms over $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is a level translate of the centre of $W_t$; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose level translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   The deck-group and crossing hypotheses are: `hn1`, `hnq`, that $1 \le n$ and $n \mid q+1$; `hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`, that $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$; `hm1`, `hm`, that $1 \le m$ and $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t' w$ for a unit $w$; `hζc`, `hζcprim`, that $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ is a unit for $0 < k < n$; `hjC`, `ha₀y`, that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ lies in the chart algebra and differs from $a_0$ by an element of $y$; `hn`, that $n = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$; `hR7`, the ends package (summarised here), which requires that $\tau_0$ acts on $B_t$ with exact order $n$, that every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ acts on $B_t$ as a power of $\tau_0$, that `ends` has $q+1$ elements permuted transitively by the level automorphisms and each preserved by $\tau_0$, that distinct ends are separated by a function which is a nonunit in one and a unit in the other, that all ends are localisations of one finite-type subalgebra stable under level automorphisms, that an automorphism mapping an end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$, that each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and Noetherian, contains the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ in $A \cap k_0$, has residue field that of $A \cap k_0$, and admits a crossing description: an isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$, carrying constants to $\mathrm{const}$ and two elements $c_x$, $c_y$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m \cdot \mathrm{unit}$ to unit multiples of the coordinates $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q - a_0$ corresponding to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, and with $\tau_0$ corresponding to an automorphism $\theta_0$ which scales $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, together with an Igusa-type separating discrete valuation subring $W_x$ and a finite-type subalgebra $B_x$ with the listed properties, and finally that a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ over $A\cap k_0$ containing the chart algebra and cutting out $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates an end; `hR9`, that some element of $B_t$ lies in no valuation subring over $A\cap k_0$ in which $\pi_0$ is a nonunit and $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental (no monic polynomial in $j_\ell$ with coefficients in $A\cap k_0$ becomes a nonunit); and `hR10`, that for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which is not the image of $y$ under any level automorphism, some element of $B_t$ is excluded from every valuation subring containing the chart algebra and cutting out $y''$ after the corresponding level automorphism.
--
--   The hypothesis `hInert` requires, for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A\cap k_0$, a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring with the kernel, scalar and level-equivariance clauses of `hS1`, and in addition an exponent $\eta \in \{1, q\}$ such that for every $\pi$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every compatible pair of automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $k_0$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A \cap k_0$ inducing the identity on the residue field, with $\sigma_A\pi = \alpha_t\pi$, every unit $\alpha$ of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ reducing to $\alpha_t$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ acting coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$: $\tau$ preserves $B_t$ and $W_t$, and for every $d \in (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image is $\alpha^{q+1}$ one has $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}\,q$ at $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^\eta)^{-1}, \alpha^\eta) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ applied to $\rho$.
--
--   Conclusion. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ consisting exactly of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$, there is a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that:
--
--   (1) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$;
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring;
--   (3) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal;
--   (4) for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ function field whose base change is an $R_0$-integer, regular at every place where $j$ is regular, and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the evaluation at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that image and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--   (5) for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f$ with both $f$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f$ in $F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$;
--   (6) there exist a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ with the following properties:
--    (6a) the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$;
--    (6b) $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-field generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a ratio of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator;
--    (6c) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--    (6d) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is a prime element of $B$; and an element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ precisely when it is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$;
--    (6e) the image of $jq$ lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for all $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--    (6f) some $b \in B \cap F_0$ lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ in $A$, in which $\pi_0$ is a nonunit, and at which $j$ is residually transcendental (no monic polynomial in $j$ with coefficients in $k_0 \cap A$ becomes a nonunit of $V$);
--    (6g) for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$, some $b \in B \cap F_0$ lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ in $A$ and satisfying the specialisation property of (4) with $s'$ and $V$ in place of $s$ and $W_0$;
--    (6h) for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q$ of that field a domain, and every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,C_s$ (the fixed field of the subgroup of $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ generated by the scalars in $C_s$) with $\#C_s = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, $\ker\rho$ the ideal generated by $\varpi_b$, $\rho$ compatible with the residue map of $A$ on $A_b$, every element of the target a ratio of two $\rho$-values, the range of $\rho$ consisting exactly of the elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field comes from the coordinate ring, and $\rho$ equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ one has $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f) = \mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q$ at that element applied to $\rho(f)$;
--    (6i) for every ring homomorphism $\iota$ of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ into $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, with the induced algebra structure and the coordinate ring a domain, there is a single subgroup $C_s$ with $\#C_s = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ such that for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ there is a $\rho$ with the five clauses of (6h) and, in addition, an exponent $\eta \in \{1, q\}$ such that for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup $A.\mathrm{inertiaSubgroupIn}\,\mathbb Q$ preserving $k_0$, every unit $\alpha$ with $\iota(\alpha) = A.\mathrm{tameCharacter}\,\pi\,\tau$, and the semilinear automorphism $g = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ at $\tau$: $g$ preserves $B$, and for every $d \in (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image is $\alpha^{q+1}$, $\rho(g \cdot f) = \mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q$ at $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^\eta)^{-1}, \alpha^\eta)$ applied to $\rho(f)$;
--    (6j) there are: the $R_0$-integrality of $j$ together with the fact that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; the membership of $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; an element $a_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q} =$ the evaluation at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with $\#\text{nodes} = q+1$, such that: there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every node, each node being a localisation of $B_c$ at its units; the maps $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ permute the nodes, and for each $\zeta$ the action on nodes is transitive; distinct nodes $O \ne O'$ are separated by an element which is a nonunit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$; every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ in $A$ and satisfying the specialisation property of (4) with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node (contains it, with its nonunits in the maximal ideal of $V$); and each node $O$ satisfies: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is local and Noetherian; $O$ meets $k_0$ in $A$; every element of $O$ differs from a constant of $k_0 \cap A$ by a nonunit of $O$; and there are a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$ together with a unit $v$ of $A$ in $k_0$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s} \cdot v$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the adic completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$, $\iota$ carries constants to $\mathrm{const}$, carries $c_x$ to $\gamma_U \cdot U$ and $c_y$ to $\gamma_V \cdot V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and $c_x$ does not, and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q - a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ with $\iota$-image a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$; furthermore there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, meeting $k_0$ in $A$, a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, admitting an element $t$ such that any polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ whose value at $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ has all its coefficients in that maximal ideal, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_x$, computing the $R_0$-residues in the sense that for every $g$ as in (4) but without the assumption on $s$, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs by a nonunit of $O$ from every constant of $k_0 \cap A$ in $O$ with matching residue; and every node other than $O$ contains an element outside $W_x$; and finally there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B \cap O$, all of whose elements are regular at every place of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ is regular, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, with $F_0$ the field of fractions of $B_x$, generated by the constants of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ in $A$, in which $\pi_0$ is a nonunit, at which $j$ is residually transcendental in the above sense, and which fails to contain all of $O$.
--
--   This is the level-descent step in the construction of the semistable supersingular charts of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H}(q^2M')$ at the prime $q = 2$, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ frame with guard prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: the rigid chart data over the small field $k_0$ (affine model, ends, crossing model, Drinfeld reduction and tame-inertia law) are transported to the field $F_0$ of Laurent series with $k_0$-coefficients inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, producing a discrete valuation ring $W_0$, an $A_b$-algebra $B$ with its Drinfeld-curve reduction and $q+1$ nodes. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
